mainmenu "Pyxis Configuration"

menu "Caelum"

config NPFS_FLUSH_SECONDS
  int "npfs background flush interval (seconds)"
  range 1 4294967
  default 30
  help
    Flush all dirty npfs data periodically. This interval is
    nominal: a flush can take longer under load. File, directory and mount
    synchronization operations provide the explicit durability guarantees.

config HPET_MAINTENANCE_TICKS
  int "HPET maintenance interval (BSP timer ticks)"
  range 1 4294967295
  default 120
  help
    Sample a software-extended 32-bit HPET after this many delivered BSP
    LAPIC timer interrupts. The current 120 Hz timer makes 120 ticks
    nominally one second. Direct 64-bit HPET counters need no maintenance.

    Choose an interval well below the hardware counter's wrap time.
    Initialization rejects a nominal interval of one wrap or longer.
    Interrupt delays also count toward the less-than-one-wrap sampling
    requirement; elapsed time always comes from HPET, not timer ticks.

config XHCI
  bool "XHCI"
  default y
  help
    Enable native xHCI controller preparation and USB enumeration.
    Enable boot-present device inventory and qualified USB storage access.

endmenu
